 "result_text": "I fixed `to_struct` in `stellar_sdk/scval.py` so it sorts the struct's field names alphabetically before building the map. I haven't run any tests or checked the fix against the network.\n\nThe cause is probably the key order. Soroban expects map keys in sorted order, and `to_struct` kept the dict's insertion order. Your struct went out as `source, asset, price, timestamp`, which isn't sorted. That would explain the \"failed to convert ScVal to host value\" error. With the change, it goes out as `asset, price, source, timestamp`. I think the fix addresses your error, but I haven't confirmed the host accepts the sorted version.\n\nI left `to_map` alone. It still keeps whatever order you pass in, so anyone building a map by hand with `to_map` still has to sort the keys themselves.",
